[{"id":"question 7471","verdict":"wrong","correct_option":2,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 36.331, the eNB uses the RRC Connection Release message with re-directedCarrierInfo IE to redirect a UE to another E-UTRAN frequency. UE CONTEXT RELEASE REQUEST (option 5) is sent eNB->MME for S1 release, not for inter-frequency redirection.","source":"3GPP TS 36.331 (RRC Connection Release with re-directedCarrierInfo)"},{"id":"question 7481","verdict":"wrong","correct_option":3,"evidence":"In TCP/IP, the server waits passively (binds and listens on a port) while the client actively initiates. Option 2 reverses these roles. Option 3 is correct: the server software does notify the application when a connection request arrives (via accept()).","source":"IBM z/OS TCP/IP docs; standard client-server model"},{"id":"question 7515","verdict":"correct","correct_option":4,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 23.002 V12.6.0 section 4.1.1.2, the VLR contains subscriber data needed for CS call handling, including the MSRN (Mobile Station Roaming Number) which is used to route calls to the actual current location of the MS. Other options describe different entities: option 1 (packet data) = SGSN; option 2 (E-UTRAN termination) = MME; option 3 (switching/signaling) = MSC; option 5 (IMSI storage) is partial.","source":"3GPP TS 23.002 section 4.1.1.2"},{"id":"question 7614","verdict":"correct","correct_option":2,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 22.011 section 3.2.2.5, periodic network selection attempts are based on PLMN priority - the UE looks for a higher priority PLMN of the same country as the currently received PLMN. 'Priority and availability of PLMNs' matches the criterion.","source":"3GPP TS 22.011 section 3.2.2.5"},{"id":"question 7998","verdict":"correct","correct_option":3,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 38.321 Table 4.5.3-1, the CCCH (Common Control Channel) is the bidirectional common control channel used for RRC messages between UE and network when no dedicated UE identity exists. BCCH (option 1) and PCCH (option 2) are downlink only.","source":"3GPP TS 38.321 section 4.5.3"},{"id":"question 8028","verdict":"correct","correct_option":2,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 23.501 section 5.11.1 NOTE 1: 'Subject to policies in the NG-RAN, configuration of Dual Connectivity for a Data Radio Bearer can also be based on the Network Slice that the PDU Session belongs to.'","source":"3GPP TS 23.501 section 5.11.1"},{"id":"question 8092","verdict":"correct","correct_option":5,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 25.430 section 5.2.2: 'Logical O&M is the signalling associated with the control of logical resources (channels, cells,...) owned by the RNC but physically implemented in the Node B. All messages needed to support this information exchange are classified as Logical O&M forming an integral part of NBAP.'","source":"3GPP TS 25.430 section 5.2.2"},{"id":"question 8120","verdict":"wrong","correct_option":1,"evidence":"Per RFC 6356, MPTCP's main mechanism is 'coupled congestion control' to achieve bottleneck fairness and resource pooling by linking subflow increase functions. Per-packet load balancing causes reordering issues and is NOT what MPTCP uses.","source":"RFC 6356 'Coupled Congestion Control for Multipath Transport Protocols'"},{"id":"question 8265","verdict":"correct","correct_option":4,"evidence":"The Transport Layer (OSI layer 4) provides reliable transmission (TCP with acknowledgments/retransmission) and end-to-end logical point-to-point connections via TCP sockets.","source":"OSI model - Transport Layer (TCP) functions"},{"id":"question 8361","verdict":"correct","correct_option":1,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 22.173 section 4.2 'Default media handling capabilities': 'The IMS Multimedia Telephony service shall support the following handling of media - Adding, removing and modifying individual media to/from a IMS Multimedia Telephony communication.'","source":"3GPP TS 22.173 section 4.2"},{"id":"question 8364","verdict":"wrong","correct_option":null,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 38.401 section 7.6, 'The NG-RAN supports the positioning functionality' as its own dedicated function (Positioning). The listed options (RACH Optimization, PCI Optimization, PTP/PTM switching, CCO, NR MBS) do not include positioning. CCO (option 4) is for coverage/capacity optimization, not positioning.","source":"3GPP TS 38.401 section 7.6"},{"id":"question 8411","verdict":"wrong","correct_option":null,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 22.011 section 4.3.3, 'Access Control for CSFB' is a distinct mechanism specifically for CSFB, but it is not listed in the options. While its criteria are equivalent to ACB (option 1), ACB applies generally to mobile-originated access, not specifically to CSFB. None of the options specifically applies to CSFB.","source":"3GPP TS 22.011 section 4.3.3"},{"id":"question 8441","verdict":"wrong","correct_option":2,"evidence":"Open-system authentication is a NULL algorithm - it provides no authentication, only identification via MAC address. Shared-key authentication proves the requesting station's knowledge of the shared secret (only the requester's identity is verified). 'Only proves the identity of one station' matches shared-key.","source":"IEEE 802.11 wireless authentication (Microsoft Learn); MIT CSAIL PARANOIA paper"},{"id":"question 8500","verdict":"wrong","correct_option":2,"evidence":"Per RFC 2131 Table 2: 'DHCPDISCOVER - Client broadcast to locate available servers.' Its main purpose is to request an IP address from available DHCP servers. Option 2 captures this standard description.","source":"RFC 2131 section 3.1 (DHCP messages table)"},{"id":"question 8636","verdict":"wrong","correct_option":1,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 36.314 section 4.1.1: 'The objective of the PRB usage measurements is to measure usage of time and frequency resources. A use case is cell load balancing.' L2 measurements support load balancing, not MIMO specifically. Option 1 is the closest purpose.","source":"3GPP TS 36.314 section 4.1.1"},{"id":"question 8745","verdict":"correct","correct_option":4,"evidence":"RSTP fast ring detection is a recognized RSTP extension used for faster recovery times in automation networks. Per Phoenix Contact FL SWITCH manual, it provides fast switch-over (100-500 ms) to a redundant path in ring configurations.","source":"Phoenix Contact FL SWITCH documentation on RSTP Fast Ring Detection"},{"id":"question 8770","verdict":"correct","correct_option":2,"evidence":"Per 3GPP TS 23.502 and Cisco AMF documentation: After purge timer expiry, AMF sends Nudm_SDM_Unsubscribe to UDM to unsubscribe from changes to subscription data, then sends Nudm_UECM_Deregistration. The unsubscribe step matches option 2.","source":"3GPP TS 23.502; Cisco AMF Network-Initiated Deregistration Request docs"},{"id":"question 8782","verdict":"correct","correct_option":1,"evidence":"Per IEEE P2061 / Frugal 5G architecture paper: 'The Flow Controller is an RACF that directly interfaces with the RSCFs.' The RAT Agnostic Control Functions (RACFs), including Flow Controller, interface with the RAT Specific Control Functions (RSCFs).","source":"IEEE P2061 Frugal 5G Architecture paper (arXiv:1902.01367)"}]